+\subsection{Evidence for the two service outputs}\label{sec:consumerproofs}
+The packages $\pi_R$ and $\pi_G$ from Section~\ref{sec:spec} collect the evidence
+used by the existing consumer checks in \cref{alg:pull}. Relative to the
+receiver's already verified history, their required components are:
+\begin{itemize}
+\item \textbf{Regional evidence $\pi_R$.} The activation record and its witness
+authorize the global view and initial $R_0$. A contiguous chain of committed
+regional records reaches an outcome covering $M_h$; each new record has its
+$\RC$ and complete batch witness. The receiver verifies original-author
+signatures, predecessor continuity and the COMMIT certificates, and checks
+that the activation's fixed start time has been reached before Preview.
+\item \textbf{Global evidence $\pi_G$.} A checkpoint covers the block in its
+adopted prefix. Its checkpoint/report transition witnesses, missing regional
+commit evidence and authority transitions establish that prefix. A
+justification chain from a trusted anchor and the adjacent finalizing link
+establish finality as specified in \cref{alg:finality}; finality of a descendant
+also finalizes its ancestors. The receiver obtains and verifies the new block
+bodies before Deliver and processes intervening activations as in
+\cref{alg:pull}.
+\end{itemize}
+Already verified objects may be referenced; a new receiver obtains the missing
+ancestry. A prepared certificate alone is insufficient for Preview, and a
+regional commit certificate alone is insufficient for Deliver. The packages
+use the portable certificate predicates of Section~\ref{sec:pbftobjects};
+they do not add a requirement to reconstruct old NEWVIEW histories.
