+ANNOUNCE advertises available data, GET requests an identified range, and DATA
+returns its content and verification evidence. The objectID identifies the
+requested protocol object; kind distinguishes the advertised object/evidence
+category. The body contains the requested records or transaction bytes, and
+the witness contains the signatures, certificates and referenced history
+needed for verification. These are abstract interfaces; the notation does not
+prescribe a serialization or an additional consensus message.
 An object identifier binds a header, range and evidence type, not a peer address.
 A supplier is free to be different from its original producer. A DATA response
 is useful only if the entire requested object verifies against that identifier
